    "title": "Express need, duty and advice",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-obligation-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Express need, duty and advice",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "必须 states a requirement. 得 pronounced děi can say have to; it differs from unstressed de after a verb. 应该 can offer advice, while 需要 can name a practical need. Read the context rather than equating every recommendation or need with an obligation.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我必须去。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ bìxū qù 。",
                "meaning": "I must go.",
                "audio": "89e650447302d57710996e7126fc4b91b70d72251a87e87d0828f4fe4a0eb141"
              },
              {
                "text": "我得去。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ děi qù 。",
                "meaning": "I have to go.",
                "audio": "4fe6911cd674dca964e5e86b6376c31afa69f154ecec8cffb94427b6246568b1"
              },
              {
                "text": "你应该看书。",
                "pinyin": "nǐ yīnggāi kàn shū 。",
                "meaning": "You should read, as advice.",
                "audio": "0457a4143d6c2491a79ca7e472b6a08908c70251b76d6abf0bbfc397b1bbf377"
              },
              {
                "text": "我需要水。",
